-- Tests for the NIS Regulations 2018 incident-notification encoding, with expected
-- values written by hand from the source text and a calendar. The arithmetic for every
-- date and time is in NOTES.md ("How the expected times were worked out"); none was
-- copied from l4's output.
--
-- DRAFT. Not for use as advice.
-- Every assertion here is expected to be satisfied. A failure is a finding.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nis-domain`
IMPORT `nis-regulations`
IMPORT `nis-seat`

-- The YMD shim: the stable prelude has no YMD (docs/ENCODING-GUIDE.md, section 5).
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
YearMonthDay y m d MEANS Date d m y -- renamed from YMD so it cannot collide with the YMD in newer daydate libraries; see docs/ENCODING-GUIDE.md section 5

§ `Fixtures`

`yes`    MEANS `yes, it is`
`no`     MEANS `no, it is not`
`unsure` MEANS `I cannot say`

`RDSP 12(3)` MEANS `regulation 12(3): an RDSP's incident`
`OES 11(1)`  MEANS `regulation 11(1): an OES's NIS incident`
`OES 12(9)`  MEANS `regulation 12(9): an OES's notice of an incident affecting an RDSP it relies on`

-- A moment on one clock.
GIVEN dt IS A DATE, h IS A NUMBER, mi IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `a moment`
`at` dt h mi MEANS
    `a moment` WITH
        `day`    IS dt
        `hour`   IS h
        `minute` IS mi

-- Asking "Do the Regulations apply to me?" with the seat's inputs, in the seat's order:
-- information society service, cloud, search engine, marketplace, provided in the UK,
-- head office in the UK, UK representative, micro or small enterprise, OES.
`a UK cloud company`            MEANS `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `yes` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `Regulation 1: am I an OES or an RDSP?`

-- A UK-headquartered, medium or large provider of a cloud computing service in the UK.
#ASSERT `a UK cloud company` EQUALS `yes, as an RDSP only`
-- None of the three kinds of digital service.
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `no` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I am neither an OES nor an RDSP`
-- The fork F1: the provider cannot say whether its AI API is a cloud computing service.
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `unsure` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `only as an RDSP, and only if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
-- The two answers to F1, tabulated: yes gives RDSP, no gives neither (the two lines above and below).
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `yes` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, as an RDSP only`
-- An online search engine, not a cloud service.
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `no` `yes` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, as an RDSP only`
-- An online marketplace.
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `no` `no` `yes` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, as an RDSP only`
-- "Cannot say" on one kind, "yes" on another: a digital service either way.
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `unsure` `yes` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, as an RDSP only`
-- Not an information society service: not a digital service, whatever its kind.
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` FALSE `yes` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I am neither an OES nor an RDSP`
-- Head office outside the UK, with a UK representative nominated: an RDSP (reg 1(3)(e)(i)).
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `yes` `no` `no` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, as an RDSP only`
-- Head office outside the UK, no representative: not an RDSP on the text as written (F7).
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `yes` `no` `no` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I am neither an OES nor an RDSP`
-- Head office in the UK and a representative too: either suffices.
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `yes` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, as an RDSP only`
-- A micro or small enterprise is not an RDSP (reg 1(3)(e)(ii)).
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `yes` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: I am neither an OES nor an RDSP`
-- Not provided in the United Kingdom.
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `yes` `no` `no` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I am neither an OES nor an RDSP`
-- An OES that is also an RDSP; an OES only; an OES that cannot say whether it is also an RDSP.
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `yes` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes, as an OES and as an RDSP`
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `no` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes, as an OES only`
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `unsure` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes, as an OES; and as an RDSP too if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
-- An OES that is a small enterprise is still an OES; only the RDSP test excludes small enterprises.
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `yes` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes, as an OES only`

§ `Regulation 14A: must I nominate a UK representative?`

-- Inputs: information society service, cloud, search engine, marketplace, offered in the
-- UK, head office in the UK, micro or small enterprise.
-- A non-UK cloud provider offering in the UK, medium or large: must nominate.
#ASSERT `must I nominate a UK representative` TRUE `yes` `no` `no` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I must nominate a UK representative in writing and notify the Information Commission of its name and contact details`
-- Head office in the UK: 14A does not apply.
#ASSERT `must I nominate a UK representative` TRUE `yes` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: regulation 14A does not apply to me`
-- A micro or small enterprise (14A(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `must I nominate a UK representative` TRUE `yes` `no` `no` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: regulation 14A does not apply to me`
-- Not offering in the UK.
#ASSERT `must I nominate a UK representative` TRUE `yes` `no` `no` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: regulation 14A does not apply to me`
-- F1 again.
#ASSERT `must I nominate a UK representative` TRUE `unsure` `no` `no` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `only if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
#ASSERT `must I nominate a UK representative` TRUE `no` `no` `no` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: regulation 14A does not apply to me`
-- Not an information society service: not a digital service provider.
#ASSERT `must I nominate a UK representative` FALSE `yes` `no` `no` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: regulation 14A does not apply to me`
-- The F7 pair, same provider: it must nominate (14A), and until it does it is not an RDSP (1(3)(e)(i)).
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `yes` `no` `no` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I am neither an OES nor an RDSP`
#ASSERT `do the NIS Regulations apply to me` TRUE `yes` `no` `no` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, as an RDSP only`

§ `Regulations 11 and 12: must I notify, and whom?`

-- The incident inputs after the nine provider inputs: actual adverse effect, substantial
-- impact (RDSP), information to assess (RDSP), significant impact on the essential
-- service (OES), an RDSP incident affecting me (OES, reg 12(9)).

-- An RDSP with an incident of substantial impact, able to assess it: notify the Information Commission.
#ASSERT `must I notify this incident` TRUE `yes` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I must notify`
#ASSERT `whom must I notify about this incident` TRUE `yes` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Information Commission`
-- Without information to assess the impact, the duty does not apply (reg 12(4)).
#ASSERT `must I notify this incident` TRUE `yes` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I need not notify under these Regulations`
#ASSERT `whom must I notify about this incident` TRUE `yes` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no one under these Regulations`
-- Not a substantial impact.
#ASSERT `must I notify this incident` TRUE `yes` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I need not notify under these Regulations`
-- No actual adverse effect: not an "incident" at all (reg 1(2)).
#ASSERT `must I notify this incident` TRUE `yes` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I need not notify under these Regulations`
-- F1 again: the duty depends on the classification the provider cannot make.
#ASSERT `must I notify this incident` TRUE `unsure` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I must notify only if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
#ASSERT `whom must I notify about this incident` TRUE `unsure` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Information Commission, if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
-- F1 answered no: nothing to notify under these Regulations.
#ASSERT `must I notify this incident` TRUE `no` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I need not notify under these Regulations`
-- An OES (not an RDSP) with a NIS incident: notify its designated competent authority.
#ASSERT `must I notify this incident` TRUE `no` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `I must notify`
#ASSERT `whom must I notify about this incident` TRUE `no` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `my designated competent authority`
-- An OES whose incident had no significant impact on continuity.
#ASSERT `must I notify this incident` TRUE `no` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I need not notify under these Regulations`
-- An OES with "significant impact" claimed but no actual adverse effect: no incident, no regulation 11 duty.
#ASSERT `must I notify this incident` TRUE `no` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `I need not notify under these Regulations`
-- An OES hit by an incident at an RDSP it relies on (reg 12(9)).
#ASSERT `must I notify this incident` TRUE `no` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `I must notify`
#ASSERT `whom must I notify about this incident` TRUE `no` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `my designated competent authority`
-- Regulation 12(9) does not bind a non-OES.
#ASSERT `must I notify this incident` TRUE `no` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `I need not notify under these Regulations`
-- An OES that is also an RDSP, both duties triggered.
#ASSERT `whom must I notify about this incident` TRUE `yes` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Information Commission and my designated competent authority`
-- An OES that cannot say whether it is an RDSP, both triggers met.
#ASSERT `whom must I notify about this incident` TRUE `unsure` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `my designated competent authority; and the Information Commission too if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
-- Neither an OES nor an RDSP (a small enterprise), every incident fact true.
#ASSERT `must I notify this incident` TRUE `yes` `no` `no` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `I need not notify under these Regulations`

§ `By when: the 72-hour outer limit`

-- Aware 2 March 2026 09:15; 72 hours on is 5 March 2026 09:15.
#ASSERT `by when must I notify` `RDSP 12(3)` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) 9 15 EQUALS JUST (`at` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) 9 15)
#ASSERT `by when must I notify` `OES 11(1)` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) 9 15 EQUALS JUST (`at` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) 9 15)
-- Over the end of February 2026 (28 days): aware 27 Feb 22:30, limit 2 March 22:30.
#ASSERT `by when must I notify` `OES 11(1)` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 27) 22 30 EQUALS JUST (`at` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) 22 30)
-- Over 29 February 2028: aware 27 Feb 10:00, limit 1 March 10:00.
#ASSERT `by when must I notify` `RDSP 12(3)` (YearMonthDay 2028 2 27) 10 0 EQUALS JUST (`at` (YearMonthDay 2028 3 1) 10 0)
-- Over the year end: aware 30 Dec 2026 18:00, limit 2 Jan 2027 18:00.
#ASSERT `by when must I notify` `RDSP 12(3)` (YearMonthDay 2026 12 30) 18 0 EQUALS JUST (`at` (YearMonthDay 2027 1 2) 18 0)
-- Regulation 12(9) states no outer limit.
#ASSERT `by when must I notify` `OES 12(9)` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) 9 15 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Both sides of the edge: aware 2 March 2026 09:15.
-- 71h59m: 5 March 09:14, in time.
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `RDSP 12(3)` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) 9 15 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) 9 14 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 72h00m: 5 March 09:15, in time ("no later than 72 hours after").
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `RDSP 12(3)` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) 9 15 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) 9 15 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 72h01m: 5 March 09:16, late.
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `RDSP 12(3)` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) 9 15 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) 9 16 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The same three for an OES's NIS incident.
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `OES 11(1)` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) 9 15 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) 9 14 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `OES 11(1)` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) 9 15 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) 9 15 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `OES 11(1)` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) 9 15 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) 9 16 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Across midnight: aware 2 March 23:30; 5 March 23:30 in time, 6 March 00:00 (72h30m) late.
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `RDSP 12(3)` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) 23 30 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) 23 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `RDSP 12(3)` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) 23 30 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 6) 0 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Over the end of February 2026: aware 27 Feb 22:30; 2 March 22:30 in time, 22:31 late.
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `OES 11(1)` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 27) 22 30 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) 22 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `OES 11(1)` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 27) 22 30 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) 22 31 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Notified within the same minute as awareness.
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `RDSP 12(3)` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) 9 15 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) 9 15 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Three calendar days later but at an earlier hour is in time; it is the hours that count, not the date.
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `RDSP 12(3)` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) 9 15 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) 8 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Regulation 12(9): no outer limit, so no answer.
#ASSERT `was my notification within 72 hours` `OES 12(9)` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) 9 15 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 9) 9 15 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulations 17 and 18: the most I can be penalised`

`no EN`         MEANS `no enforcement notice was served on me`
`EN no steps`   MEANS `an enforcement notice was served on me but required no steps`
`EN steps done` MEANS `an enforcement notice required steps and I took them within its period`
`EN steps not done` MEANS `an enforcement notice required steps and I did not take them within its period`
`significant`   MEANS `the authority determines it has or could have created a significant risk to, or significant impact on, my service provision`
`not significant` MEANS `the authority determines it does not meet that test`
`undetermined`  MEANS `the authority has not yet determined this`
`reading A`     MEANS `reading A: a late notice is a failure to notify under regulation 12(3)`
`reading B`     MEANS `reading B: lateness alone is not a failure regulation 17(2) lists`
`did not notify` MEANS `I did not notify at all`
`notified late`  MEANS `I notified, but more than 72 hours after the clock started`
`no information` MEANS `I notified in time, but without the required information`
`all well`       MEANS `I notified in time with the required information`

-- An OES that did not notify, no enforcement notice: a material contravention (18(7)(a)(ii)).
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `OES 11(1)` `did not notify` `reading A` `no EN` `significant` EQUALS `up to 17,000,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines has or could have created a significant risk to, or significant impact on, my service provision`
#ASSERT `the ceiling in pounds` (`what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `OES 11(1)` `did not notify` `reading A` `no EN` `significant`) EQUALS JUST 17000000
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `OES 11(1)` `did not notify` `reading A` `no EN` `not significant` EQUALS `up to 8,500,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines does not meet regulation 18(6)(d)`
#ASSERT `the ceiling in pounds` (`what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `OES 11(1)` `did not notify` `reading A` `no EN` `not significant`) EQUALS JUST 8500000
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `OES 11(1)` `did not notify` `reading A` `no EN` `undetermined` EQUALS `up to 8,500,000 pounds, or up to 17,000,000 pounds if the authority determines it has or could have created a significant risk to, or significant impact on, my service provision`
#ASSERT `the ceiling in pounds` (`what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `OES 11(1)` `did not notify` `reading A` `no EN` `undetermined`) EQUALS JUST 17000000
-- An OES that notified late (a failure under 11(3), listed in 17(1)(c)); enforcement notice steps not taken: material (18(7)(a)(i)).
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `OES 11(1)` `notified late` `reading B` `EN steps not done` `significant` EQUALS `up to 17,000,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines has or could have created a significant risk to, or significant impact on, my service provision`
-- The same, but the steps were taken in time: not a material contravention, so 1,000,000 pounds whatever the authority's view (F9).
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `OES 11(1)` `notified late` `reading B` `EN steps done` `significant` EQUALS `up to 1,000,000 pounds: not a material contravention`
#ASSERT `the ceiling in pounds` (`what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `OES 11(1)` `notified late` `reading B` `EN steps done` `significant`) EQUALS JUST 1000000
-- An OES whose notice lacked the required information; an enforcement notice required no steps: material (18(7)(a)(ii)).
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `OES 11(1)` `no information` `reading A` `EN no steps` `not significant` EQUALS `up to 8,500,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines does not meet regulation 18(6)(d)`
-- An RDSP that notified late: the fork F3, both readings.
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `RDSP 12(3)` `notified late` `reading A` `no EN` `significant` EQUALS `up to 17,000,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines has or could have created a significant risk to, or significant impact on, my service provision`
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `RDSP 12(3)` `notified late` `reading B` `no EN` `significant` EQUALS `no penalty under regulation 18 on reading B: lateness alone is not a failure regulation 17(2) lists`
#ASSERT `the ceiling in pounds` (`what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `RDSP 12(3)` `notified late` `reading B` `no EN` `significant`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- An RDSP that did not notify at all: listed (17(2)(b)) on either reading.
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `RDSP 12(3)` `did not notify` `reading B` `no EN` `significant` EQUALS `up to 17,000,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines has or could have created a significant risk to, or significant impact on, my service provision`
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `RDSP 12(3)` `did not notify` `reading A` `no EN` `undetermined` EQUALS `up to 8,500,000 pounds, or up to 17,000,000 pounds if the authority determines it has or could have created a significant risk to, or significant impact on, my service provision`
-- An RDSP whose notice lacked the required information (17(2)(c)), enforcement notice steps taken: 1,000,000 pounds.
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `RDSP 12(3)` `no information` `reading A` `EN steps done` `not significant` EQUALS `up to 1,000,000 pounds: not a material contravention`
-- An RDSP whose notice was short of the cross-border information 12(6)(b) requires: the F3 readings again.
`cross-border short` MEANS `I notified in time with the regulation 12(5) items, but not enough for the Information Commission to determine the significance of any cross-border impact (regulation 12(6)(b))`
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `RDSP 12(3)` `cross-border short` `reading A` `no EN` `significant` EQUALS `up to 17,000,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines has or could have created a significant risk to, or significant impact on, my service provision`
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `RDSP 12(3)` `cross-border short` `reading B` `no EN` `significant` EQUALS `no penalty under regulation 18 on reading B: a regulation 12(6)(b) shortfall alone is not a failure regulation 17(2) lists`
#ASSERT `the ceiling in pounds` (`what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `RDSP 12(3)` `cross-border short` `reading B` `no EN` `significant`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 12(6)(b) binds only an RDSP.
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `OES 11(1)` `cross-border short` `reading A` `no EN` `significant` EQUALS `not answered here: regulation 12(6)(b) binds only an RDSP`
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `OES 12(9)` `cross-border short` `reading A` `no EN` `significant` EQUALS `not answered here: regulation 12(6)(b) binds only an RDSP`
-- No failure: no penalty.
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `RDSP 12(3)` `all well` `reading A` `no EN` `significant` EQUALS `no penalty: there was no failure to notify`
#ASSERT `the ceiling in pounds` (`what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `RDSP 12(3)` `all well` `reading A` `no EN` `significant`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Regulation 12(9): a failure to notify at all is listed (17(1)(d)); lateness and content are not answered here.
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `OES 12(9)` `did not notify` `reading A` `no EN` `not significant` EQUALS `up to 8,500,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines does not meet regulation 18(6)(d)`
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `OES 12(9)` `notified late` `reading A` `no EN` `significant` EQUALS `not answered here: regulation 12(9) sets no 72-hour clock and no list of contents`
#ASSERT `what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `OES 12(9)` `no information` `reading A` `no EN` `significant` EQUALS `not answered here: regulation 12(9) sets no 72-hour clock and no list of contents`
